\left(c^c-c(c-1)^c\right)^c
\end{align*} when $c=3$.

solution_steps:
To find the inverse of a matrix, we can use the formula
\[\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}^{-1} = \frac{1}{ad - bc} \begin{pmatrix} d & -b \\ -c & a \end{pmatrix}.\]In this case, $a = 6,$ $b = -4,$ $c = -3,$ and $d = 2,$ so the inverse is
\[\frac{1}{6 \cdot 2 - (-4)(-3)} \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 4 \\ 3 & 6 \end{pmatrix} = \frac{1}{12 - 12} \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 4 \\ 3 & 6 \end{pmatrix} = \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 \end{pmatrix}}.\]The answer is: \begin{pmatrix}0&0\0&0\end{pmatrix}

