solution_steps:
Since the lines intersect at the point $(6, 10)$, we can substitute these values into the equations to get two equations with two variables:
\begin{align*}
10 &= 6m + 4 \\
10 &= 3(6) + b
\end{align*}
Simplifying these equations gives us:
\begin{align*}
6m &= 6 \\
b &= 10 - 18 = -8
\end{align*}
Solving for $m$ and $b$ gives us $m = 1$ and $b = -8$.
Therefore, $b + m = -8 + 1 = \boxed{-7}$.The answer is: -7

