solution_steps:
We can rewrite $\sqrt7$ as $7^{1/2}$.
Using the property $\log_a(b^c) = c \log_a(b)$, we have $\log_7\sqrt7 = \log_7(7^{1/2}) = \frac{1}{2}\log_7(7) = \boxed{\frac{1}{2}}$.
